Date: Sat, 6 Jun 2026 10:54:56 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] fix: synchronize PalettedContainer.copy for atomic snapshot

copy() read data/palette/storage without holding the container monitor
that set/onResize/write all synchronize on. The off-thread anti-xray
section copy could capture a torn snapshot (palette from before a
resize, storage from after), producing an unparseable chunk packet so
the client hung forever on 'loading terrain' for any ore-bearing chunk.
Mark copy() synchronized to match the other accessors.

diff --git a/net/minecraft/world/level/chunk/PalettedContainer.java b/net/minecraft/world/level/chunk/PalettedContainer.java
index 66a05adab494f8674f0636f8b34533f8ef640028..832c5260d804edeeaf97ee2c6eb004b3b30bf88e 100644
--- a/net/minecraft/world/level/chunk/PalettedContainer.java
+++ b/net/minecraft/world/level/chunk/PalettedContainer.java
@@ -406,7 +406,7 @@ public class PalettedContainer<T> implements PaletteResize<T>, PalettedContainer
     }
 
     @Override
-    public PalettedContainer<T> copy() {
+    public synchronized PalettedContainer<T> copy() { // Leaf - synchronize: copy must read data/palette/storage atomically vs set/onResize/write (off-thread anti-xray section copy was reading a torn snapshot -> unparseable chunk packet)
         return new PalettedContainer<>(this, this.presetValues); // Paper - Anti-Xray - Add preset values
     }
 
